5. Epistemic Separation

Type	Meaning	Fact status

FACT	Established under applicable evidence rules	May become authoritative
OBSERVATION	Directly observed/recorded	Evidence-bearing
INFERENCE	Derived conclusion	Not fact by default
HYPOTHESIS	Proposed explanation/prediction	Never fact
COUNTERFACTUAL	Alternative outcome not observed	Never fact
SIMULATION	Generated result under assumptions	Research evidence only


This distinction is mandatory.

A simulated result cannot accidentally become a historical observation.


