9. Versioned Knowledge

Knowledge can evolve:

BELIEF B

V1
 ↓
V2
 ↓
V3
 ↓
CURRENT

But the previous versions are not deleted.

Example:

2027:
"Company financial position appears strong."

2028:
"New evidence weakens that conclusion."

2029:
"Earlier conclusion was partially incorrect because receivable quality was misunderstood."

CNS retains the evolution.

This allows CNS to know:

what it believed

why it believed it

what changed

what evidence caused the change

whether the previous reasoning failed



