13. Coverage and Contradiction

Coverage is measured against the evidence required for the task, not merely against database size.

Example:

If CNS investigates a company, required dimensions might include:

Financials
Management
Industry
Competition
Valuation
Customers
Debt
Cash flow
Related parties
Legal/regulatory
Historical behavior
Risks

If only 4 are available:

Coverage = insufficient

CNS should know what is missing.

That missing coverage can trigger additional work through 3C.

Contradictions

CLAIM A
   ↕
compare:
subject
time
scope
provenance
epistemic type
   ↕
CLAIM B

Result:

COMPATIBLE
CONTEXTUAL DIFFERENCE
CONTRADICTION
UNRESOLVED

Contradictions are investigation signals, not values to average away.


