16. Retention and Archive

State	Meaning

RETAIN_PERMANENT	Critical evidence, decisions, outcomes, provenance
RETAIN_CHEAPLY	Useful but rarely accessed
ARCHIVE	Preserved in low-cost storage
COMPRESS	Reduced representation while auditability remains
SUPERSEDED	Newer version replaced it; history retained
INVALID	Known invalid but retained as useful failure evidence
DELETE	Only under explicit retention/legal/storage policy


Important

A wrong conclusion can still be extremely valuable.

For example:

> "CNS believed X in 2028 and was wrong."



That is experience.

So we don't simply erase it.


