18. Consistency, Concurrency and Crash Recovery

Memory write:

MEMORY WRITE
 ↓
validate expected version
 ↓
append authoritative event
 ↓
transactional state update
 ↓
commit
 ↓
asynchronous index update
 ↓
retrieval visibility

If crash occurs:

DURABLE EVENT
 ↓
REPLAY
 ↓
REBUILD STATE / INDEX

Rules:

durable state/event is authoritative

indexes are derived

concurrent writes cannot silently overwrite each other

conflicts become explicit versions

retries are idempotent

crash recovery uses replay



